@participant2 Exactly. The `ExponentImagePicker.launchImageLibraryAsync()` promise is handled by the `catch`.

```
    const options = {
      mediaTypes: ImagePicker.MediaTypeOptions.Images,
      allowsEditing: false,
      exif: true,
      quality: 0.91,
    };

    ImagePicker.launchImageLibraryAsync(options)
    .then(() => {})
    .catch(() => {
        // here
    })
```

So, it nevers shows up because the logic behind showing the photo is handled in the `then`

